          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with typical absence seizures, beginning at age 23. The epilepsy is drug responsive. MRI demonstrates MOGHE, consistent with a structural etiology.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Zonisamide  \n- Perampanel  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nCurrently seizure-free, with 0 seizures per month.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-responsive generalized epilepsy with typical absence seizures and structural etiology associated with MOGHE on MRI. Seizures remain controlled on the current regimen.\n\n**Plan:**  \n- Continue zonisamide and perampanel.  \n- Continue monitoring seizure burden.  \n- Follow up in the epilepsy clinic.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
